.\" Man page for codebundler. Mirrors the man page shipped in the published
.\" 1.0.0 deb (generated there by scdoc); here it is plain roff so it can be
.\" committed and installed straight to ${CMAKE_INSTALL_MANDIR}/man1.
.TH "CODEBUNDLER" "1" "2026-10-12" "CodeBundler 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
codebundler \- bundle source files into one shareable artifact
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B codebundler
.B bundle
.I [output_file] [options]
.PP
.B codebundler
.B unbundle
.I [input_file] [output_dir] [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B codebundler
bundles the tracked files of a project into a single artifact (with SHA256
checksums per file) so it can be shared as one file — for example, pasted to
an AI assistant.
.B unbundle
verifies the checksums and restores the file tree.
.PP
Bundling writes to stdout if no output file is given; unbundling reads from
stdin if no input file is given and extracts to the current directory if no
output directory is given. The separator is detected automatically from the
first line of a bundle.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B bundle
.I [output_file]
Bundle the tracked files of the current project.
.TP
.B unbundle
.I [input_file] [output_dir]
Extract files from a bundle, verifying SHA256 checksums.
.SH BUNDLE OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-separator
.I <sep>
Use a custom separator string (default "========= BOUNDARY ==========").
.TP
.B \-\-description
.I <desc>
Add an optional description to the bundle header.
.SH UNBUNDLE OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-verify
Disable SHA256 checksum verification.
.TP
.B \-\-trial\-run
Perform a trial run without writing files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose
Enable verbose output (repeat for more detail).
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Bundle the current repository to a file and restore it elsewhere:
.PP
.RS
codebundler bundle /tmp/project.bundle
.br
cd /elsewhere && codebundler unbundle /tmp/project.bundle .
.RE
.PP
Pipe through stdin/stdout:
.PP
.RS
codebundler bundle | ssh host codebundler unbundle
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/HarryPehkonen/CodeBundler
